## fm-brief.sh renders a forge=gitlab ship brief (direct-PR, with a base branch)
$ fm-brief.sh brief-dpr firstmate-gitlab-port-fixture --mode direct-PR --forge gitlab --base-branch develop
scaffolded: $LAB/data/brief-dpr/brief.md (ship, mode=direct-PR forge=gitlab; replace {TASK} and {FIRSTMATE_SPEC})
[exit 0]
$ grep -nE 'Delivery contract|glab-axi|gh-axi|target-branch|Base branch' $LAB/data/brief-dpr/brief.md
17:Base branch: develop
30:3. Use glab-axi for GitLab operations, gh-axi for GitHub operations, and chrome-devtools-axi for browser operations.
92:Delivery contract: mode=direct-PR forge=gitlab
96:When it is implemented and committed, push your branch and open a merge request with `glab-axi` that is ready for review, not a draft, against the base branch `develop` (`--target-branch develop`), not the repository default.
97:Before you report done, read the merge request back from the forge and confirm it is not a draft (`glab-axi mr view <iid> --full` must print `draft: no`, where <iid> is the merge request number from your MR URL); if it is a draft, mark it ready with `glab-axi mr update <iid> --ready`.
[exit 0]
## no-mistakes forge=gitlab brief: the pipeline publishes, the readback uses glab-axi
$ fm-brief.sh brief-nm firstmate-gitlab-port-fixture --mode no-mistakes --forge gitlab
scaffolded: $LAB/data/brief-nm/brief.md (ship, mode=no-mistakes forge=gitlab; replace {TASK} and {FIRSTMATE_SPEC})
[exit 0]
$ grep -nE 'Delivery contract|glab-axi|gh-axi' $LAB/data/brief-nm/brief.md
30:3. Use glab-axi for GitLab operations, gh-axi for GitHub operations, and chrome-devtools-axi for browser operations.
94:Delivery contract: mode=no-mistakes forge=gitlab
129:After /no-mistakes reports CI green (the CI-ready return point - do not wait for it to keep monitoring in the background until merge), read the PR back from the forge and confirm it is not a draft (`glab-axi mr view <iid> --full` must print `draft: no`, where <iid> is the merge request number from your MR URL); if it is a draft, mark it ready with `glab-axi mr update <iid> --ready`.
[exit 0]
## adversarial: forge composition guards
$ fm-brief.sh brief-lo firstmate-gitlab-port-fixture --mode local-only --forge gitlab
error: fm-brief.sh --forge: forge=gitlab cannot ship mode=local-only - that mode publishes nothing, so a forge has no meaning there, and its landing would fast-forward local main with content the review server has never seen; ship no-mistakes or direct-PR, which publish through the forge
[exit 1]
$ fm-brief.sh brief-ge firstmate-gitlab-port-fixture --mode direct-PR --forge gerrit --base-branch develop
error: fm-brief.sh --base-branch: a base branch is not supported on forge=gerrit
[exit 1]
$ fm-brief.sh brief-bad firstmate-gitlab-port-fixture --mode direct-PR --forge gitlb
error: fm-brief.sh --forge: unknown forge 'gitlb' (expected none, gerrit, gitlab, or forgejo)
[exit 1]
